 "summary": "The workhorse segment. Reabsorbs about 65% of filtered Na⁺ and water (isotonically), about 85% of HCO₃⁻, almost all glucose and amino acids and most phosphate; makes NH₄⁺ (ammoniagenesis) and secretes organic anions and drugs. Angiotensin II stimulates NHE3; PTH inhibits Na⁺–phosphate cotransport. Drugs: acetazolamide (carbonic anhydrase), SGLT2 inhibitors. Generalized failure is Fanconi syndrome; failure to reclaim HCO₃⁻ is proximal (type 2) renal tubular acidosis.",
 "tissue": "kidney: proximal convoluted tubule (cortex)",
 "icon": "water_drop",
 "color": "gold",
